{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\n`store_freshness` reports `stale-store` from a **persisted sentinel** that is never checked\nagainst observable git state. Once any ticket-branch push fails, the sentinel sticks, and\nevery plan-review and completion gate in that clone refuses to decide — permanently — even\nafter the events have demonstrably been delivered.\n\n## Observation\n\nIn `.rebar/worktrees/fix-985f-sandbox/.tickets-tracker`, after a successful manual push,\n`git rev-parse HEAD origin/tickets` printed the SAME commit\n(`9a10e59a2a825d071f5e1780dc362c7aacfb3cc2`) and `git status -sb` showed no ahead/behind.\nYet `rebar review-plan concise-deplorable-gerenuk --status` returned\n`{\"ok\": false, \"verdict\": \"stale-store\"}`, claiming \"5 committed ticket event(s) the shared\nstore has never received (last delivery failure: push-transport-failed)\". The claim of 5\nundelivered events is false, and the count is itself stale: after a later write the same\nprobe reported 1 while the refs were again level.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `src/rebar/_store/freshness.py`, `store_freshness` consults the sentinel only after the\ndivergence branch declines:\n\n```python\nstatus = push_state.read_status(tracker)\npending = status.get(\"state\") == \"pending\"\n...\nif divergence is not None:\n    ...\nelif pending:\n    verdict = \"push-pending\"\n```\n\n`_ref_divergence` (`freshness.py:66-92`) returns `None` for **both** \"level\" and \"strictly\nahead\" — its docstring says so. So when refs are level, control falls to `elif pending` and\nthe persisted sentinel decides the verdict unchallenged. The sentinel is cleared only by a\nrebar-performed push (`push.py:254`, `push.py:290`). Recovering by hand\n(`git push origin HEAD:tickets`) delivers the events and leaves the sentinel set forever.\n\n`_ref_divergence` already computes the evidence needed to falsify the sentinel; it discards\nthe level-vs-ahead distinction before the sentinel is consulted.\n\n## Why this is worth fixing rather than tolerating\n\nThe module docstring states the design intent: \"a broken diagnostic must never be able to\nblock a healthy gate,\" and the probe deliberately degrades to `fresh` on any internal\nfailure. A false `stale-store` on a provably level store is the exact failure that contract\nexists to prevent.\n\n## Approach\n\nDistinguish **level** from **ahead** in `_ref_divergence`, and treat a level store as proof\nof delivery: when `origin/tickets` and `HEAD` are the same commit there are no undelivered\nevents, so the sentinel is stale and is reconciled rather than reported.\n\n### The write, its failure behaviour, and its ownership\n\nReconciling clears the persisted marker via `push_state.clear`, which **never raises** — it\nswallows `FileNotFoundError` and logs any other error at debug (`push_state.py:187-198`). A\nclear that fails therefore leaves the marker in place and the probe still returns `fresh`\nfor this call, so the fail-open contract is preserved by construction and no new failure\nmode reaches the caller.\n\nThe clear condition is identical to the one existing clear outside the push path,\n`completion_delivery.py:294-301`, which clears only when `local_oid == remote_oid` under the\ncomment \"a different local HEAD can belong to a concurrent writer whose delivery outcome we\ndo not own.\" This change adopts that same equality rule, so the ownership discipline is\nunchanged: clearing happens only when the remote ref already contains every local commit.\n\nThat equality is also what makes the concurrent-writer race benign. A rebar push writer sets\nthe marker only after a push FAILED, and at that moment HEAD is ahead of the remote-tracking\nref, so the probe computes ahead > 0 and does not clear. For the probe to clear, the\nremote-tracking ref must already hold every local commit — under which the marker's own claim\n(\"committed events the shared store has never received\") is false whichever writer set it.\nThe probe remains no-fetch, so it reads the same `origin/tickets` ref the divergence check\nalready trusts; a stale ref can only make the probe UNDER-report ahead-ness, which is a\npre-existing property of every comparison in this function rather than something introduced\nhere.\n\n### Rejected\n\n- **Clearing the sentinel on any read.** Loses the genuine push-pending signal for a clone\n  that really is ahead.\n- **Making the probe fetch.** The docstring is explicit that it is purely local and must\n  never make a gate depend on network reachability.\n- **Documenting a manual reset command.** Leaves a correct-by-inspection store reporting\n  itself broken, and puts the burden on whoever hits it next.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression test drives a tracker into `push_state` pending, brings HEAD level with\n      `origin/tickets`, and asserts `store_freshness` returns verdict `fresh`, added to\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py`.\n- [ ] That same test is recorded failing on baseline `main` before the fix, with the\n      `stale-store` verdict quoted on this ticket.\n- [ ] A clone genuinely AHEAD of `origin/tickets` with the sentinel set still reports\n      `push-pending`, asserted by its own test so the fix cannot whitewash undelivered events.\n- [ ] The existing cases in `pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py` pass unchanged,\n      covering the behind verdict via `test_a_store_behind_the_shared_store_is_stale`, the\n      diverged verdict via `test_a_diverged_store_is_stale`, and the fail-open contract via\n      `test_the_probe_fails_OPEN_on_its_own_error`.\n- [ ] The sentinel is reconciled rather than ignored: after one level-store probe, a second\n      `push_state.read_status` call reports state `ok`, asserted in the same test.\n- [ ] A test asserts that when `push_state.clear` cannot remove the marker, the probe still\n      returns `fresh`, proving the write cannot make the diagnostic block a healthy gate.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0, with the exit code recorded on this ticket.\n\n## Testing\n\n`pytest tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py` covers the ref states (level, ahead, behind,\ndiverged) crossed with the sentinel set and unset, the reconciliation assertion that a second\n`push_state.read_status` reports state `ok`, and the fail-open assertion that a failing clear\nstill yields `fresh`. `make verify` is the pre-push gate and must exit 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789871440692687188,"uuid":"5d387ca7-7dce-4350-b838-87827159de4a"}